Ship, Captain, and Crew is a popular dice game that can be played with two or more players. The objective of the game is to roll a specific combination of dice to score points and become the player with the highest score at the end of the game.

Here are the rules to play Ship, Captain, and Crew:

1. Each player rolls five dice on their turn. The objective is to roll a 6 (the "ship"), a 5 (the "captain"), and a 4 (the "crew") in any order.
2. Once a player has rolled a ship, captain, and crew, they can set those dice aside and roll the remaining dice to try to get the highest possible score.
3. The player's score is the sum of the remaining dice. For example, if a player rolls a 6, 5, 4, 3, and 2, and sets aside the 6, 5, and 4, their score would be 3 + 2 = 5.
4. If a player does not roll a ship, captain, and crew on their first roll, they can choose to set aside any dice they want and reroll the remaining dice up to two more times.
5. If a player is unable to roll a ship, captain, and crew after three rolls, their turn ends and they score zero points.
6. The game continues with each player taking turns until every player has had an equal number of turns. The player with the highest total score at the end of the game wins.
7. In case of a tie, the tied players continue to take turns until one player has a higher score than the others.

That's all there is to it! The game is simple, but it can be quite exciting as players try to roll the elusive ship, captain, and crew combination and rack up the highest possible score.

